    "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Permutation Given Using Alternate Notation",
    "problem": "Evaluate $P(6,3).$",
    "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(6,3)$ means the same thing as ${}_{6}{P}_{3}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(6,3) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6!}{3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
